- Agents do very well with 'making it all work' even in very complex setups as long as they have been used to do the work end to end. They share context and decisionmaking information between sessions very smoothly, but get confused more quickly once they are collaborating alongside humans.
- It's easy to forget that agents need very explicit coaching not to be bastards; despite very clear and even LLM-targeted terms of use on [Nominatim's](https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/) docs & general coaching to the agents I've been using that they are staff software engineers working for a civic group, the agent suggested pulling them in for exactly the autocomplete address purpose they forbid. It very diligently planned around the api limits put in place to prevent abuse like this. You have to be extremely explicit with agents, and always review the docs for third parties yourself.
